<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Repository-level NuGet configuration.

  Why this exists: Bindings.csproj sets IsAotCompatible, which pulls in
  Microsoft.NET.ILLink.Tasks as an implicit package reference. Restoring it failed with
  NU1100 - "Unable to resolve 'Microsoft.NET.ILLink.Tasks (>= 11.0.0-preview.7.26381.103)'
  for 'net11.0'. PackageSourceMapping is enabled, the following source(s) were not
  considered: Microsoft Visual Studio Offline Packages, nuget.org."

  The package is not missing: it is on nuget.org at exactly that version. It was filtered
  out by a machine-level packageSourceMapping whose patterns do not match
  Microsoft.NET.ILLink.*. Because that config lives outside the repository, a checkout
  would build or not build depending on the machine. This file makes the answer the same
  everywhere.

  On the wildcard pattern: source mapping exists to stop a public package shadowing one
  from a private feed. This repository configures exactly one source, so there is nothing
  to shadow and the mapping is not a weakening. If a private feed is ever added here,
  replace the wildcard with explicit patterns per source before doing so.

  This affects no repository other than this one. NuGet reads configs from the project
  directory upward, and settings closer to the project win.
-->
<configuration>
  <packageSources>
    <!-- clear drops inherited sources so a build here does not depend on machine state. -->
    <clear />
    <add key="nuget.org" value="https://api.nuget.org/v3/index.json" protocolVersion="3" />
  </packageSources>

  <packageSourceMapping>
    <!-- Also cleared: an inherited mapping is what caused NU1100. -->
    <clear />
    <packageSource key="nuget.org">
      <package pattern="*" />
    </packageSource>
  </packageSourceMapping>
</configuration>
